===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*kh₂eyd-}}
{{uder|en|la|caesūra||cutting, hewing}}, from {{m|la|caesus}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|caedō||I cut down, hew}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/sɪˈzjʊəɹə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/sɪˈʒʊɹə/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-caesura.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʊəɹə|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|caesurae}}
{{anchor|pause}}

# A [[pause]] or [[interruption]] in a [[poem]], [[music]], [[building]], or [[other]] [[work]] of [[art]].
# {{lb|en|Classical [[prosody]]}} Using two words to divide a [[metrical]] [[foot]].
# {{lb|en|typography}} The [[#pause|caesura]] [[mark]] '''[[‖]]''' or '''||'''.
# {{lb|en|rarely}} A break of an era or other measure of history and time; where one era ends and another begins.

====Usage notes====
In poetry bearing caesuras, it is marked by a double vertical line.

====Synonyms====
